<urn:usf:requirement:atlas-capture-v3-timing:3> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Every job records UTC start/end, monotonic clock and fractional-or-null elapsed milliseconds, finite action, bound source asset IDs, configured limits and result. Command identity is only approved logical executable ID, raw argv digest and argument count. Closed environment identity records clock, network state, cgroup control names and control/membership digests plus host-tooling digest; unavailable values remain null or unknown. Raw argv, arbitrary environment values and absolute paths are not portable output. A configured CPU quota is not measured CPU time." <urn:usf:graph:atlas-capture-symbol-assurance-observer> .
